local _, ns = ...

ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "6.1.1", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• Minimap: |cffffffffAddons in the Drawer|r (all), under |cffffffffAddon Button Drawer|r: tick the addons whose buttons go in the drawer. The others are left alone on the minimap, where their addon puts them. Changes take effect after a reload.\n      - It replaces Shift+Right-Click on drawer icons, which clashed with addons' own right-click menus. Buttons you kept on the minimap that way stay out of the drawer.\n• Settings › Sync Blizz UI: |cffffffffHide Pop-up Alerts|r (off): syncs still happen, with no pop-up asking to reload, on every character. The pop-up's new |cffffffffHide These Alerts|r button turns it on.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Minimap, square style: addon buttons left out of the drawer sit on the border, packed along the bottom from beside the sundial. Drag one along the border and it stays where you drop it, through every reload. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap, square style: the bronze border is drawn under the map, so no addon button can end up beneath it.\n• Unit frames › player frame › Visibility: |cffffffffMissing Health|r and |cffffffffMissing Mana|r can no longer be ticked together; ticking one unticks the other. The game hides both from addons, so the two can't be combined. If you had both, Missing Mana stays. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: |cffffffffActive Highlight|r follows the button's own frame, round corners and all, instead of a square. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: the |cffffffffMiddle-Click Menu|r opens again. Other clicks ping the map as usual. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: addon buttons no longer move around on every reload, and RareScanner's button shows again when left out of the drawer. Thanks for the report!\n• Resource bars: Blizzard's own swing timer no longer appears in busy fights when FlareUI's swing bars are on. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames: the player frame now fades as it should with Missing Health and Missing Mana both set (see Changed). Thanks for the report!" },
    { version = "6.1", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders|r is now its own page, with much more to track: talent buffs, weapon oils and stones, elixirs, supplies, durability and your own custom reminders.\n• |cffffffffMouseover|r is now a Visibility condition you tick, so bars and frames show on hover only when you want them to.\n• |cffffffffTooltips|r get a Visibility tab: when each kind shows, and which ones follow your mouse.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Buff Reminders: its own page in the Combat group, with its own switch. Your settings carry over.\n      - |cffffffffReminders|r tab: Class Buffs, Weapons, Consumables, Upkeep and Your Own.\n      - |cffffffffWhen and Where|r tab: when a buff counts as running out, where each kind shows, and which group buffs to hide.\n      - |cffffffffAlerts|r tab: |cffffffffSound|r and |cffffffffReady Check Alert|r.\n      - Its Edit Mode window gains |cffffffffAlerts|r (|cffffffffGlow When Missing|r, |cffffffffGlow When Running Out|r, |cffffffffTime Left|r) and |cffffffffHide While Mounted|r.\n      - It no longer needs Buffs & Debuffs to be on.\n• Buff Reminders: talent and class buffs, once you know the spell. Thanks for the request!\n      - Priest: |cffffffffDivine Spirit|r on your group, and |cffffffffShadowform|r (not while you're the healer).\n      - Druid: |cffffffffOmen of Clarity|r. Hunter: |cffffffffTrueshot Aura|r and an |cffffffffAspect|r reminder (a click puts your last one back).\n      - Warlock: |cffffffffSoul Link|r while your pet is out, and a |cffffffffSoulstone|r on your group's healer.\n      - Warrior: |cffffffffBattle Shout|r on you and your party.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffExtra Buffs|r (none) adds |cffffffffShadow Protection|r and |cffffffffMoonkin Form|r when ticked.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffWeapon Oil / Stone|r (off), for every class. Click to use one from your bags; right-click to pick which. Sharpening stones go on blades, weightstones on maces and staves.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffPlaystyle|r (Automatic) picks which oil or stone comes first: stones for melee and tanks, wizard oil for casters, mana oil for healers.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffElixirs and More|r: tick the elixirs, Zanza, juju and Blasted Lands buffs you want kept up. Click to use one from your bags.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffLow Supplies|r (off) for reagents and ammo, |cffffffffLow Durability|r (off) below 20%, and |cffffffffWorn Trinkets|r (off) for an Argent Dawn trinket or Carrot on a Stick still on in a dungeon or raid.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffAdd Custom Reminder|r: your own reminder by spell name or ID, or an item. Right-click its icon to remove it.\n• Buff Reminders: right-click an icon to |cffffffffSnooze Until Recast|r.\n• Buff Reminders: where each kind shows: |cffffffffClass Buffs|r, |cffffffffWeapon Buffs|r, |cffffffffPets|r and |cffffffffConsumables|r, each Always, In Dungeons and Raids, or In Raids.\n• Buff Reminders: icons that use an item show how many you have; a buff running out shows its time left; a poison low on charges counts as running out.\n• Tooltips: a |cffffffffVisibility|r tab.\n      - |cffffffffVisibility|r: World, Unit Frames, Action/Data Bars, Buffs/Debuffs, Party/Raid Auras and the new |cffffffffEverything Else|r (the minimap, menus and more): Always, Hide in Combat or Never.\n      - |cffffffffMouseover|r: which of them appear at your mouse. Each follows the main |cffffffffMouseover|r on the Settings tab; a change here is an exception for that kind. Thanks for the request!\n• Edit Mode › player frame › Fading: |cffffffffLink Pet Frame|r (off): the pet frame fades with the player frame, and pointing at either shows both. Thanks for the idea!\n• Bags & Looting: |cffffffffOpen with Character Window|r (off): your bags open and close with the character window. Thanks for the request!\n• Bags & Looting › Fonts: |cffffffffFree Bag Slots|r (Default): the font of the free-slot count on the backpack button. Thanks for the request!\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Visibility: |cffffffffMouseover|r is now a condition you tick with the others, on every faded bar and frame and on Fake CM. Without it, pointing at a faded frame doesn't show it.\n      - If you had conditions set, Mouseover is ticked for you, so nothing changes until you untick it.\n      - Nothing ticked now means Always.\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffAnchor|r is now |cffffffffMouseover|r, a switch on the Settings tab for every tooltip at once. Your choice carries over.\n• Bags & Looting: the bank and guild bank now open your bags, as the vendor and mailbox do.\n• Minimap: the |cffffffffMiddle-Click Menu|r works as before 6.0.3 again: a middle click opens the menu without a ping, and the square map's corners ping. In battlegrounds the game keeps the map's clicks to itself, so there's no menu there.\n• Loot Feed: money shows just the coins you looted, without the gold icon. Thanks for the request!\n• Unit frames: in the ring styles, Target of Target and Target of Focus have their portrait on the left, so the bar runs left to right clear of it.\n• Radial menu: the catalog's sections stay on one line, and an empty catalog says why.\n• Buff Reminders: Food and Flask is a switch, with its place under When and Where.\n• Buff Reminders: an oil or stone on a warlock's weapon no longer brings up the Firestone reminder. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Action bars: |cffffffffActive Highlight|r no longer leaves spells like Rend or Thunder Clap lit after you use them. Thanks for the report!\n• Buffs: a sharpening stone's or oil's icon no longer disappears after you die. Thanks for the report!\n• Buff Reminders: food buffs not called \"Well Fed\" (Nightfin Soup, Grilled Squid and more) count, and Demonic Sacrifice no longer asks for your pet.\n• Edit Mode: FlareUI's loot rolls, toasts and other frames keep working after an update read with /reload; FlareUI now tells you to restart instead. Thanks for the report!\n• Radial menu: the |cffffffffProfessions|r catalog finds your professions.\n• Settings: longer translations fit their buttons, and the About page scrolls. Thanks to parchinskiy!" },
    { version = "6.0.3", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffffffPlease check your settings.|r Some defaults changed in this version (listed under |cffffffffDefaults|r). Options you already set yourself keep your choice; options you never touched take the new default.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting|r is now its own page, with its own switch.\n• |cffffffffFlight Timer|r and |cffffffffPaladin Seals|r: two new resource bars.\n• |cffffffffWeapon buffs|r in Buff Reminders: warlock stones, off-hand weapons, and clicks that put poisons and imbues on the right hand.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Bags & Looting: a page of its own, out of Quality of Life.\n      - |cffffffffBags|r tab: |cffffffffBag Window|r, |cffffffffItem Slots|r and |cffffffffTools|r sections.\n      - |cffffffffLooting|r tab: |cffffffffFaster Auto Loot|r, |cffffffffSkip Loot Confirmations|r and the |cffffffffLoot Feed|r.\n      - |cffffffffFonts|r tab: |cffffffffBag Items|r and |cffffffffLoot Feed|r.\n      - Your settings carry over. Its switch starts on if you had Quality of Life on.\n• Bags & Looting › Bags: |cffffffffCategory Filters|r (off). A button beside the cleanup button opens a drawer: |cffffffffQuest Items|r, |cffffffffEquipment|r, |cffffffffMaterials|r or |cffffffffConsumables|r. Everything else dims. Right-click the button to clear it. Thanks to parchinskiy for the idea!\n• Bags & Looting › Fonts: |cffffffffBag Items|r (Default) sets the font of the stack counts and cooldown numbers on your bag items.\n• Resource bars: |cffffffffFlight Timer|r (off). A bar while you're on a flight path, with where you're going and the time left.\n      - Each route is learned the first time you fly it. Until then the bar counts up.\n      - Learned times also show on the flight map when you point at a destination.\n• Resource bars: |cffffffffPaladin Seals|r (off). One bar with your seal's name and time left, in that seal's own colour. Pick each seal's colour in |cffffffffBar Colours|r.\n• Buff Reminders: weapon buffs. Thanks for the report!\n      - Warlocks: a |cffffffffFirestone|r or |cffffffffSpellstone|r reminder. Click to make one, or to put one from your bags on your weapon.\n      - Off-hand weapons get their own reminder, for rogues and dual-wielding shamans.\n      - Only your class's own weapon buff counts: a sharpening stone no longer hides a poison or imbue reminder.\n      - Rogues: click to put a poison from your bags on that hand.\n      - Shamans: click to put the imbue on that hand.\n      - Right-click an icon to pick which poison, imbue or stone goes on each hand (|cffffffffLast Used|r by default).\n• Action bars: |cffffffffActive Highlight|r (off), in |cffffffffButton Appearance|r. Your stance or form, a queued Heroic Strike, Cleave, Maul or Raptor Strike, and a repeating Auto Shot get a gold edge and a light. Queued attacks pulse. Thanks for the request!\n• Action bars › XP Bar: |cffffffffShow Bubbles|r (off) divides the XP, reputation and honor bars into 20 parts, like the classic bar. Thanks to mateuszmalek!\n• Edit Mode: Blizzard's |cffffffffTotem Bar|r gets |cffffffffSize|r and a |cffffffffFading|r section with fade groups, like the action bars. Thanks for the request!\n• Minimap: |cffffffffFramerate|r (off): your framerate at the bottom right of the map, |cffffffffAlways|r or |cffffffffOn Mouseover|r. Thanks for the request!\n• Damage Meter: |cffffffffFade Delay|r (Instant), after |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r: how long the meter stays before it fades.\n• Radial menu: drag radials in the |cffffffffRadials|r list to reorder them.\n• Radial menu: |cffffffffgroups|r. Right-click a radial to |cffffffffAdd to New Group...|r, move it to a group or take it out.\n      - Click a group's row (or its |cffffffff+ / −|r) to fold or open it.\n      - Right-click a group to |cffffffffRename...|r or |cffffffffUngroup|r it.\n      - Drag radials into a group, and drag a group to move it.\n• Radial menu: a |cffffffffProfessions|r catalog with your professions and Smelting, Disenchant, Find Herbs, Find Minerals, Basic Campfire and Pick Lock.\n• Fonts: every font on every |cffffffffFonts|r tab has a |cffffffffReset|r button.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit frames and resource bars: |cffffffffColour Palette|r is now |cffffffffFrame Colours|r and |cffffffffBar Colours|r: a |cffffffffPick Your Colours|r button you always see.\n      - In its window, the palette list at the bottom offers |cffffffffFlareUI|r (default), |cffffffffBlizzard|r and |cffffffffCustom|r.\n      - Change any colour and the palette becomes |cffffffffCustom|r. |cffffffffReset|r gives your colours back.\n      - |cffffffffApply|r saves and closes. Closing with unsaved colours asks whether to keep them.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffCoordinates on Mouseover|r is now |cffffffffCoordinates|r: |cffffffffOff|r, |cffffffffAlways|r or |cffffffffOn Mouseover|r. It is the same option as Blizzard's own coordinates. If you had Coordinates on Mouseover off, you get |cffffffffAlways|r.\n• Minimap: the addon drawer's |cffffffffOpen on Mouseover|r closes sooner after the pointer leaves.\n• Quest tracker: |cffffffffColour Names by Difficulty|r is now |cffffffffColour by Difficulty|r.\n• Loot Feed: a single item shows just its name, and several show \"Name x3\". Thanks to Nico-Mayer!\n• Radial menu: a new radial is available to |cffffffffAll Characters|r by default.\n• Radial menu: |cffffffffQuest Items|r has a new icon.\n• Settings: options reordered on the Action Bars, Minimap, Quest Tracker, Tooltips and Damage Meter pages, so related ones sit together.\n• Quality of Life has a new icon; the bag icon went to Bags & Looting.\n\n|cffffd100Defaults|r\n• On: |cffffffffParty Frames|r and |cffffffffRaid Frames|r (with Unit Frames), Buffs & Debuffs |cffffffffTimer Colour|r and |cffffffffArrival Animation|r, Damage Meter |cffffffffPull Warning|r and |cffffffffPull Aggro Line|r.\n• Off: Action bars |cffffffffStop Auto-Add Spells|r, Minimap |cffffffffMiddle-Click Menu|r, Quest tracker |cffffffffCompleted Last|r and |cffffffffAuto Minimize in Instances|r, Tooltips |cffffffffShow Threat|r, |cffffffffMap Pins on \"/way\"|r, |cffffffffGamepad Mode Prompt|r, and every bag option.\n• Chat, Damage Meter and Quest Tracker: |cffffffffFrame Opacity|r 60%.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffCoordinates|r On Mouseover.\n• New default spots for Buff Reminders, toasts, loot rolls, Combo Points, the swing timers and the new bars.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Minimap: clicking the map in a battleground no longer causes a blocked-action error. Thanks for the report!\n• Quest tracker: |cffffffffSort By|r By Zone no longer reorders quests by distance as you move. Thanks for the report!\n• Quest tracker: |cffffffffWrap Long Text|r no longer cuts off a longer objective. Thanks to parchinskiy!\n• Gamepad UI: settings dropdowns opened with the mouse no longer cause an error. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: with |cffffffffClean Keybind Text|r off, long key names stay on one line instead of covering the icon. Thanks for the report!\n• Radial menu: the |cffffffffAvailable To|r list of a new radial opens over its popup, not under it.\n• Radial menu: the selected button's highlight in the |cffffffffButtons|r list sits centred." },
    { version = "6.0.2", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Player frame: |cffffffffMissing Mana|r in its |cffffffffVisibility|r list (Edit Mode). Tick it with |cffffffffMissing Health|r and the frame shows while either bar is below full. Thanks for the request!\n• Quality of Life › Fonts: |cffffffffZone Text|r (Default) changes the font of the zone name that appears as you enter a new area. Its size stays Blizzard's. Thanks for the request!\n• Quality of Life › Hide Clutter: |cffffffffFlag Carrier Frames|r (off) hides the two flag carrier frames under the minimap in battlegrounds. Thanks for the question!\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: |cffffffffAuto Paging for Stealth|r is now |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r (off). The game now turns Action Bar 1 to its stealth page by itself; this option keeps your normal buttons instead. Thanks for the report!\n      - Druids keep their Cat Form page while prowling.\n      - If you had Auto Paging for Stealth off, Keep Page 1 in Stealth starts on.\n• Action bars: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r is now off by default. Turn it on in |cffffffffBar Appearance|r.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Player cast bar: your casts never turn grey. Thanks for the report!\n      - |cffffffffRange Check|r is gone from the cast bar: with it off, every cast turned grey.\n      - Blizzard's own cast bar keeps its normal colour for your casts too.\n• Action bars: a hidden |cffffffffStance Bar|r stays hidden in combat. It came back, for example when Stealth came off cooldown, until the fight ended. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: with |cffffffffKeep Bar 1 in Stances|r, the spellbook's \"not on your bars\" glow matches the bar you see. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: addon buttons you keep on the minimap with the addon drawer sit above the map border. Thanks for the report!\n• Russian: the Damage Meter's |cffffffffThreat|r tab and the |cffffffffOpen Configuration|r button in Blizzard's options no longer show squares. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings: slider values such as |cffffffffDefault|r next to Bags › |cffffffffColumns|r no longer get cut off in long translations. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames, FlareUI Style: the last bit of shadow at the top of the portrait ring is gone.\n• Radial menu: a |cffffffffParty Spell|r slice shows the spell's name while you're alone, not your own name." },
    { version = "6.0.1", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r follows Blizzard's own Cooldown Manager switch. While the Cooldown Manager is off, FlareUI leaves it alone and the option is greyed out. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings: a tab's NEW badge sits centred on the tab's top edge.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Player cast bar: your own casts keep their normal colour. Some spells turned the bar grey, whatever |cffffffffRange Check|r was set to. Thanks for the report!\n• Nameplates: with |cffffffffHide Level|r, crowd control icons sit right beside the health bar again, without a gap. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames, FlareUI Style: the portrait ring's rim is clean at the bottom, and nothing shows through beside the portrait.\n• Settings: long translations, such as Russian, no longer run past buttons, card titles, section headers or the page list. Text wraps, then shrinks to fit." },
}
